-- title:
--   Read place is a moduli place of the Frobenius-twisted fibre
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. For a field $F$ over $K$, a `Place` of $F$ over $K$ is a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$ whose ideals are principal; it is rational when $K$ surjects onto its residue field, and `evalAt` sends an element of the valuation subring to the element of $K$ with the same residue (and anything else to $0$).
--
--   **Data at $q$ and the reduction $R_0$.** Fixed are a prime $q\ge 5$, a natural number $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa_A$ for the residue field of $A$. The field `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A\,M'$ is $\kappa_A(j(\mathsf q),j(\mathsf q^{M'}))$ inside Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, and `jGeomGen` $\kappa_A\,M'$ is its generator $j(\mathsf q)$. A finite set $W$ of places of this field over $\kappa_A$ is given, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M'` $\kappa_A$: those $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace` $\kappa_A\,M'$, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of $j(\mathsf q)$ in the set `ssJSet q` $\kappa_A$. One element $s$ of $W$ is fixed. The hypothesis `hle` asks that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of $\mathbb Q(j(\mathsf q^d):d\mid M')$, be contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the function field of level $q^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH q M'` $=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\bigr)$ of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $A$ with values in $\kappa_A(j(\mathsf q),j(\mathsf q^{M'}))$: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism onto that field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places, and the axioms that an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when it lies in $A$, that residues are compatible with the residue map of $A$, that every nonzero element becomes an element of `R₀.integers` with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant, that `placeMap` preserves degrees, and that `placeMap` pushes principal divisors forward correctly. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires in addition that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **The local base.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ are given; write $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ (`A.comap` of the inclusion). The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` say that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` says that every element of $A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0\cap A$.
--
--   **The second prime and the function field $K$.** A prime $\ell'\neq q$ with $\ell'\ge 3$ and $\ell'\nmid M'$ is given, together with $\xi\in k_0$ a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity and a ring embedding $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$. Further, $K$ is an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq$ Laurent series over $k_0$, and `hK` identifies it with the $k_0$-base change of the level $(q\ell')^2M'$ function field attached to `levelH (q * ℓ') M'` $=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times\bigr)$; $K$ is an $A_0$-algebra in a way compatible with $A_0\to k_0\to K$. Finally $j\in K$ is nonzero and its underlying Laurent series is the image of the classical $q$-expansion $j(\mathsf q)$ under the coefficient embedding. Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin` $A_0\,K\,j$ for the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A_0[j]$.
--
--   **Functoriality inputs for the rigid moduli datum.** The hypothesis `hℓ` says that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, variable change $C$ and `LevelPData` $D=(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$, the predicate `IsLevelPStructure` at $\ell'$ is preserved by the simultaneous action on $W$ and $D$; `hM` says the same for `IsGamma0PowAt` and the transformation `kernelVariableChangeDeg` of kernel polynomials in degree `gamma0PowDeg p k`. Further, $\mathcal G$ is a family `GroupLaws` $A_0$ of relative group laws on the Proj models of projective Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras, with `h𝒢` (`IsChordTangent`: the group law is computed by a bijection between sections over fields and affine points, additively and Galois-equivariantly) and `h𝒢O` (`IsOriginIdentity`: the identity section is presented by a homomorphism from the origin chart ring killing $x/y$ and $z/y$). Then $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport` $A_0\,\mathcal G\,q$, that is, a functorial transport of raw Drinfeld pairs (a projective curve with two sections) along $A_0$-algebra maps and variable changes preserving the Drinfeld basis condition of level $q$, and `h𝒯` (`IsSectionTransport`) says the transported sections agree with the originals after composing with the morphisms of Proj induced by variable-change, respectively coefficient, homomorphisms. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every variable change and every $A_0$-algebra map, a graded ring homomorphism between the homogeneous coordinate rings of the corresponding Proj models, satisfying the containment of irrelevant ideals and `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   Let $\mathcal R:=$ `rigidDataPow` $A_0\,\ell'\,M'\,q$ (with `hℓ`, `hM`, $\mathcal G$, $\mathcal T$) be the resulting rigid Weierstrass datum: a raw point over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with a polynomial $h_p\in T[X]$ for each prime $p\mid M'$ satisfying `IsGamma0PowAt` for $(p,v_p(M'))$, a `LevelPData` satisfying `IsLevelPStructure` at $\ell'$, and a raw Drinfeld pair of level $q$ for $\mathcal G$; points are raw points modulo variable change, and `jOf` is the $j$-invariant.
--
--   **The representing package and the Tate point.** $P_0$ is a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for $\mathcal R$: an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ with a point `P₀.univ` over $B_0$ such that every point of $\mathcal R$ over every $A_0$-algebra is the image of `P₀.univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra map. A point $x_0$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ is given with `hx₀`: its $j$-invariant is $j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'})$. An $A_0$-algebra map `clC` $:B_0\to C$ is given with `hclC`: composed with $C\subseteq K$ it is the classifying map `P₀.classify x₀`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hμ` pins $x_0$ at the Tate point: there are a variable change $C'$ over the Laurent series field of $k_0$ and a raw representative $r$ of $x_0$ such that (i) the class of $r$ is $x_0$; (ii) with $(x_{\mathrm{tor}},y_{\mathrm{tor}})$ the cusp point `cuspPoint` $k_0\,(q\ell')$ at the unit determined by $\xi$ and the vector $(1,0)$, one has $C'.u\,(2x_{\mathrm{tor}}+\tfrac16)=2y_{\mathrm{tor}}+x_{\mathrm{tor}}$, $C'.r=-\tfrac1{12}$, $C'.s=-\tfrac12$, $C'.t=\tfrac1{24}$; (iii) the curve of $r$ becomes $C'\cdot$ `tateBase` $k_0\,(q\ell')$ over the Laurent series field; (iv) for every prime $p\mid M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring map $f:k_0\to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta$ in $F'$, the image of the $\Gamma_0$-polynomial $r.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ under $K\to$ Laurent series over $k_0\to$ Laurent series over $F'$ equals `kernelVariableChangeDeg` for the transported $C'$ in degree `gamma0PowDeg` $p\,v_p(M')$ applied to $\prod_{a}\bigl(X-(\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,(q\ell')\,\zeta^a)_1\bigr)$, the product over $1\le a\le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p\nmid a$; (v) the image of the level-$\ell'$ datum $r.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ is the variable change by $C'$ of `cuspData` $k_0\,(q\ell')$ at the vectors $(q,0)$ and $(0,-q)$; and (vi) there are $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y\in K$ whose images are the four coordinates of the variable change by $C'$ of `cuspData` $k_0\,(q\ell')$ at the vectors $(\ell',0)$ and $(0,-\ell')$, and the two Drinfeld sections $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.P$ and $Q$ pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   **The residue-field map.** Finally $\theta$ is a ring homomorphism from the residue field of $A_0$ to $\kappa_A$, and `hθ` says it is compatible with the two residue maps, i.e. $\theta$ of the residue of $a\in A_0$ is the residue in $\kappa_A$ of the image of $a$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses, the following holds for every maximal ideal $y$ of $C$, every $A_0$-algebra map $\psi:C\to$ (residue field of $A_0$) whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$ (that is, $\psi(c)=0$ iff $c\in y$), every raw point $x$ of $\mathcal R$ over the residue field of $A_0$ whose class is the image of `P₀.univ` under $\psi\circ$ `clC`, subject to the further conditions that the curve of $x$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point (every point $P$ with $q\cdot P=0$ is $0$), every point $g$ on the affine curve of $x$ satisfying `hg`, namely that $g$ has exact order $M'$ and that for every prime $p\mid M'$, every $n$ and every affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ with nonsingularity witness, if $n\cdot g=(x_1,y_1)$ and $n\cdot g$ has order $p^{v_p(M')}$ then $x_1$ is a root of the $\Gamma_0$-polynomial $x.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$, and every place $r$ of $\kappa_A(j(\mathsf q),j(\mathsf q^{M'}))$ over $\kappa_A$ which is rational and whose valuation subring contains $j(\mathsf q)$, provided $r$ reads $y$ in the following sense: for every $g_f\in\mathbb Q(j(\mathsf q^d):d\mid M')$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `R₀.integers`, which is cusp-regular in the sense that every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with non-negative order at the image of $j(\mathsf q)$ has non-negative order at the image of $g_f$, and for which the substitution $\mathsf q\mapsto\mathsf q^{\ell'}$ of the image of $g_f$ lies in $K$ and in $C$, the $R_0$-residue of $g_f$ lies in the valuation subring of $r$ and $\theta\bigl(\psi(\text{that element of }C)\bigr)=r.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g_f$.
--
--   Then there exists a place $r'$ of `modularFunctionFieldFullC` $\kappa_A\,M'$ $=\kappa_A(j(\mathsf q^d):d\mid M')$ over $\kappa_A$ such that:
--
--   1. the pullback of the valuation subring of $r'$ along the inclusion $\kappa_A(j(\mathsf q),j(\mathsf q^{M'}))\subseteq\kappa_A(j(\mathsf q^d):d\mid M')$ is the valuation subring of $r$; and
--
--   2. using that $\kappa_A$ has characteristic $q$ (which follows from `hA`), `IsModuliPlaceOf` $\kappa_A\,M'$ holds for $r'$ and for the moduli point obtained by transporting, along $a\mapsto\theta(a)^q$ (the composite of $\theta$ with the $q$-power Frobenius of $\kappa_A$), the class of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-pair consisting of the curve of $x$, with its unit discriminant, and the point $g$ of exact order $M'$.
--
--   Here `IsModuliPlaceOf` $\kappa_A\,M'$ of a moduli point and a place $v$ means that there are a field $\Omega$ over $\kappa_A$ and a `ModuliTestDatum` for that moduli point over $\Omega$ — a place $\mathcal W$ of $\Omega$ over $\kappa_A$, a Weierstrass curve over its valuation subring whose reduction has nonzero discriminant, a point of exact order $M'$ on its generic fibre, a $\kappa_A$-retraction of the residue field of $\mathcal W$ under which the reduction of the pair gives back the moduli point, and a $\kappa_A$-algebra embedding of $\kappa_A(j(\mathsf q^d):d\mid M')$ into $\Omega$ sending each generator to the $j$-invariant of the quotient of the curve by the cyclic subgroup generated by the corresponding multiple of the point — such that $v$ is the pullback of the valuation subring of $\mathcal W$ along that embedding.
--
--   This is the moduli-theoretic identification of the place that the rigid integral chart reads at a supersingular point of the special fibre: the place $r$ extends to a place $r'$ of the all-divisors level-$M'$ field which is a moduli place, in the test-datum sense, of the Frobenius twist of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-class of the fibre $(E,g)$ at the chosen maximal ideal. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_injective_forall_place_eq_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_injective_forall_place_eq_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.natCard_variableChange_act_curve_eq_and_level_fst_eq_eq_two_mul_placeWidthChar_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.natCard_variableChange_act_curve_eq_and_level_fst_eq_eq_two_mul_placeWidthChar_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint).
